  abstract={This Innovative Practice Full Paper presents detailed information about a summer camp program aimed at introducing middle school students to computing and sciences. Our program aims to inspire and empower middle school students in our region by providing opportunities to explore sciences and computing, fostering their knowledge and interest in these fields. This paper presents a comprehensive overview of the design, organization, core curriculum, and assessment of our summer camp program, offering valuable insights for educators and organizers planning similar sciences and computing outreach initiatives. It details the structure and instructional approach of the program, including a summary of the teaching materials, key concepts covered in each hands-on session, and the methods used to assess student engagement and learning outcomes. By providing a thorough blueprint for implementing similar programs, this paper serves as a practical guide for those seeking to inspire and equip the next generation of STEM learners. Additionally, it underscores the importance of expanding access to sciences and computing education and highlights the broader goal of fostering long-term interest and participation in STEM careers.},
